 raised the waistline all the way up to  just under the bust  with the gown then flowing down loosely  from that point  sorry elsa no slinky skin skimming skirt  for you  and certainly no leg slit you can keep  the cape  but we just need to make some  adjustments rather than gauzy  it would have been made from thicker  embellished fabric  and forget about the off the shoulder  neckline you need puffed up sleeves  covering your shoulders please  as for hairstyles women of a certain age  wouldn't have worn their  locks in a hanging braid back then that  style was reserved for the privacy of  their bed chamber  in public elsa would have worn her hair  up in a fancy do  much like the style she rocked at her  coronation regency's style is much more  demure but  we can't help but love elsa's ice palace  cabaret style  of course we can't include elsa and not  include anna  but to keep things interesting we've  analyzed what her more casual outfit  would have looked like  disney didn't stray too far from the  traditional folk fashion of norway at  the time  but there are a few changes we need to  make to really nail the historical  accuracy  first of all ana's trademark cloak isn't  typical of that region or that time  women wore layers to stay warm so we  need to thicken it up  and make it into a practical shawl  instead her black bodice  is more swedish than norwegian she would  have worn  a white blouse with a colorful high  collared woolen jacket over the top she  would have worn a neck scarf too  that would have come in handy on her  trip to the north mountain after all  as for her skirt she wouldn't have had  all that fancy floral embroidery  it would have more likely been simply  striped with a bit of a decorative trim  at the hem  we need to switch on his boots which  women didn't wear  for patterned stockings and flats to  finish let's give anna instant hair  extensions  she can keep the braids that's the style  young unmarried women wore  but they never cut their 